    "body": "### Description\r\n\r\n<!-- Describe the purpose of this PR, what's being adding and/or fixed -->\r\n\r\n-----\r\nThis licensing scheme gives maximum flexibility for downstream users. Apache 2.0 includes an explicit patent grant and retaliation clause, which protects users from patent litigation. With dual MIT and Apache-2.0 licensing, the user may choose any of these two at their discretion.\r\n\r\nThis is a well established standard in the rust-bitcoin and Rust ecosystems:\r\n\r\n    [getfloresta/Floresta](https://github.com/getfloresta/Floresta)\r\n    [mit-dci/rustreexo](https://github.com/mit-dci/rustreexo)\r\n    [bitcoindevkit/bdk](https://github.com/bitcoindevkit/bdk)\r\n    [lightningdevkit/rust-lightning](https://github.com/lightningdevkit/rust-lightning)\r\n    [rust-lang/rust](https://github.com/rust-lang/rust)\r\n    [rust-lang/cargo](https://github.com/rust-lang/cargo)\r\n\r\nIf you're on the below list and agree with this change please add a comment with\r\n\r\n>I hereby re-license my previous contributions to cdk under [Apache 2.0](https://choosealicense.com/licenses/apache-2.0/) in addition to the existing [MIT](https://choosealicense.com/licenses/mit/) license.\r\n\r\n- [x] @0xEgao\r\n- [x] @0xLucqs\r\n- [x] @4xvgal\r\n- [x] @AbdelStark\r\n- [x] @aki-mizu\r\n- [x] @asmogo\r\n- [x] @b-l-u-e\r\n- [x] @benthecarman\r\n- [ ] @biluohc\r\n- [ ] @black5box\r\n- [x] @callebtc\r\n- [ ] @cjbeery24\r\n- [ ] @coderwander\r\n- [x] @codingpeanut157\r\n- [ ] @DanielUhlik\r\n- [ ] @davidcaseria\r\n- [x] @daywalker90\r\n- [ ] @delcin-raj\r\n- [x] @findingsov\r\n- [ ] @gandlafbtc\r\n- [ ] @Gudnessuche\r\n- [ ] @heathermm55\r\n- [ ] @hidewrong\r\n- [x] @Jeezman\r\n- [ ] @juejinyuxitu\r\n- [x] @KnowWhoami\r\n- [ ] @Kodylow\r\n- [ ] @lorenzolfm\r\n- [ ] @luozexuan\r\n- [ ] @mountdisk\r\n- [ ] @mubarak23\r\n- [x] @ngutech21\r\n- [x] @nodlAndHodl\r\n- [ ] @ok300\r\n- [x] @Olexandr88\r\n- [x] @omahs\r\n- [x] @optout21\r\n- [x] @prusnak\r\n- [ ] @pycanis\r\n- 